SECTION 29 SUMMARY: A/B COMPARTMENT METHYLATION MAPPING
================================================================================

Input: 104071 HOMER 25kb bins -> 22143 deduplicated genes -> 16094 matched to DMRs

--- Compartment Distribution ---
  A compartment: 12351 genes (76.7%)
  B compartment: 3743 genes (23.3%)

--- Key Fisher's Test Results ---
  mC hyper -> A enriched: OR = 13.68 (11.95-15.71), p < 2.2e-16
  mC hypo -> B enriched: OR = 1.73 (1.58-1.89), p < 2.2e-16
  hmC hypo -> A enriched: OR = 9.73 (8.79-10.79), p < 2.2e-16
  hmC hyper -> B enriched: OR = 3.02 (2.72-3.35), p < 2.2e-16

--- Wilcoxon Tests (mC/hmC difference by compartment) ---
  mC A vs B: p < 2.2e-16 (median A: 0.0107, B: -0.0042)
  hmC A vs B: p < 2.2e-16 (median A: -0.0133, B: -0.0001)

--- PC1 x mC Correlation ---
  Spearman rho = 0.368, p < 2.2e-16

--- Biological Interpretation ---
  RESULT: BAP1-KO methylation changes show A/B compartment asymmetry
  consistent with the Lopez-Moyado TET-KO signature.
  This supports CONVERGENT MECHANISMS: BAP1 loss -> TET impairment ->
  DNMT3A redistribution from B (heterochromatin) to A (euchromatin).

  Plots saved to: /expanse/lustre/projects/csd940/zalibhai/mariner_hi-c/biomodal/downstream/plots/visualizations/29_ab_compartment_methylation
